WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.780
Speaker 1: We're going to talk now about the
right wing media propaganda cycle.

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:11.090
This is not dissimilar to money laundering
in a sense, where the money starts dirty and

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:12.190
ends up clean.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:15.940
Maybe not a perfect analogy, but let's think
through the cycle.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:24.310
How does the right force nonsense and imaginary
issues into what we might call the mainstream

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:26.210
of the political media discussion?

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:34.310
The first step is get some coverage of your
crazy idea or claim somewhere, even if it

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:37.500
is not reporting it as if it's true.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:42.810
But reporting that you said it either way
is good and it starts the propaganda cycle.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:48.699
So it might start, for example, in a small
local news outlet of some kind.

00:00:48.699 --> 00:00:53.559
Maybe you'll have a local reporter tweeting
about it, and often it will come from some

00:00:53.559 --> 00:00:57.129
kind of small time news agency, often understaffed.

00:00:57.129 --> 00:01:00.149
They don't have the resources to fact check
every story.

00:01:00.149 --> 00:01:04.439
They've got tight deadlines and pressure from
editors, so they've got to pump stuff out.

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:09.670
So if you can plant a rumor on one of those
platforms, you're already well on your way

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:13.740
to starting this cycle of right wing propaganda.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:17.409
And this could be, you know, there are there
are cat litter boxes in the bathrooms at some

00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:20.150
schools for the students who identify as cats.

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:22.000
That's that's one possibility.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.220
Get something written about it somewhere,
get tweets from reporters, even if it's just

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:29.860
it is being claimed that this is going on.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:37.080
The second step is you take those tweets or
local news articles or whatever the case may

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:45.159
be, and you then use social media to amplify
it based on those initial bits of reporting.

00:01:45.159 --> 00:01:49.049
You use that to generate more attention about
it, because as we know, there are so many

00:01:49.049 --> 00:01:53.689
people on Twitter that if they see Marjorie
Taylor GREENE or whoever retweet something

00:01:53.689 --> 00:01:58.770
that says they've got cat litter boxes in
schools for students who identify as cats,

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:02.610
95% of the people who see it and retweet it
won't check.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:04.030
What is the original source?

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:10.620
My I always tell you critically analyze primary
sources to try to understand what you're being

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:11.650
fed.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:17.269
You can use that initial thing to then amplify
it on social media, and then it'll take on

00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:18.269
a life of its own.

00:02:18.269 --> 00:02:23.130
Social media becomes a great breeding ground
for amplifying rumor and conspiracy theory.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:27.690
Even better, if you know how to use bots and
trolls, you can get the rumors to spread like

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:28.690
wildfire.

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:32.380
And before you know it, they've gone viral
on Twitter, on Reddit, wherever the case may

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:33.590
be.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:41.520
Step three is you want to upgrade the credibility
of the propaganda through an outlet, like

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:47.150
maybe an oann or a Newsmax, with the goal
of eventually getting it onto Fox News, where

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:53.140
the likes of Tucker Carlson can bring it up,
not yet reporting on it, but asking questions.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.140
Right.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:59.940
And this is a classic propaganda technique,
starts with some local news story based on

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:03.860
conjecture, amplified on social media by Republicans.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:11.770
And then Tucker says, listen, we need to be
allowed to ask questions about cat button

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:14.120
cat litter boxes in school bathrooms.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:20.220
The American people have a right to know about
cat litter boxes in bathrooms, and the left

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:22.030
doesn't want to talk about it.

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:25.680
Well, maybe the left doesn't want to talk
about it because there's no evidence that's

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.629
the third step in the cycle.

00:03:27.629 --> 00:03:29.410
We need to be allowed to talk about this.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:33.849
And if you can argue that someone is trying
to stop you from talking about it, even better,

00:03:33.849 --> 00:03:39.400
then you get to the fourth step, which is
sort of what we saw yesterday in the hearing

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.110
from which we saw clips earlier in the show
with Marjorie Taylor.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:48.360
GREENE Politicians need to start demanding
answers and maybe they'll hold a hearing.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:52.180
And instead of actually asking questions,
they just rant and rant and rant.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.840
And it's all because the public has a right
to know.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:59.069
And this is where these propaganda stories
can really gain momentum once politicians

00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:01.110
get involved in a formal way.

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:05.910
The rumor is now a story, even if it was always
based on nothing and the media can't ignore

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:06.910
it.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:10.180
In this case, it's about, you know, York has
lied and all these different things.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:17.100
The last step is you cement the rumor for
an election cycle by just sort of keeping

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.079
it going long enough.

00:04:19.079 --> 00:04:21.919
And that's when it becomes fact in the minds
of many people.

00:04:21.919 --> 00:04:26.790
The longer you can keep it in the news cycle,
the more that a large portion of.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:29.220
The electorate will believe that it is true.

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:33.710
It starts to be referred to as truth, and
then it can last an entire election cycle

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:34.770
or longer.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:39.210
There are so many causes of this propaganda
cycle.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:44.960
But Marjorie Taylor GREENE has added this
new layer, which is you just yell the conspiracy

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:49.550
theories that a witness to whom you're supposed
to be asking questions.

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:52.419
That is now the epitome of this.

00:04:52.419 --> 00:04:54.180
So what should we do?

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:55.410
What can we do?

00:04:55.410 --> 00:05:01.729
The most important thing is to understand
the cycle and remember if everybody understood.

00:05:01.729 --> 00:05:05.130
Critically analyze primary sources before
you.

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:08.660
Retweet, before you fall for it, before you
start talking about it as if it's true.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:13.610
If everybody understood that if we were vigilant,
if we actually tried to understand where we

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:18.240
are getting these claims from, we would be
able to short circuit these propaganda cycles

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:19.370
getting going in the first place.

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:24.259
Of course, due to a lack of media literacy,
hyper partizanship and lack of of education

00:05:24.259 --> 00:05:28.419
and so much ignorance that we see, it's very
hard to short circuit it.

00:05:28.419 --> 00:05:31.150
But this is the anatomy of that cycle.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:35.900
And Marjorie Taylor GREENE sort of knows how
to take advantage of it, that's for sure.

